    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/mckendree/jobs/5152481/adjunct-faculty-for-school-of-business-adjunct-cybersecurity-coach-computer-sc": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty for School of Business (Adjunct Cybersecurity Coach – Computer Science/Cyber Defense",
      "description": "Adjunct Faculty for School of Business (Adjunct Cybersecurity Coach – Computer Science/Cyber Defense Salary See Position Description Location Lebanon, IL Job Type Adjunct Faculty Job Number 202500094 Department Academic Affairs Division School of Business Opening Date 11/24/2025 FLSA Exempt Description Benefits McKendree University, located in Lebanon, IL and home of the Bearcats, invites qualified applicants to join our team. McKendree University offers a competitive compensation and benefits package and the opportunity to influence the future leaders of tomorrow. The mission of McKendree University is to provide a high-quality educational experience to outstanding students. We guide our students in the pursuit of academic excellence, which will prepare them for leadership roles in our society. To achieve this end we encourage broader vision, enriched purpose, engagement with community, commitment to responsible citizenship, openness to new ideas and dedication to lifelong learning. In keeping with our history and traditions, we provide our students with a rigorous, broadly based liberal arts curriculum joined with specialization in a specific discipline. Position Summary and Key Responsibilities McKendree University seeks a Cybersecurity Coach and Adjunct Instructor to support the Cyber Defense program within the School of Business. The successful candidate will: Serve as the faculty coach for the university’s Capture the Flag (CTF) and other cybersecurity competition teams. Provide mentoring, training, and coordination for student participation in regional and national cybersecurity competitions . Assist in the design, setup, and maintenance of a cybersecurity practice and testing range , including virtualized environments for teaching and competition preparation. Collaborate with faculty and IT staff to ensure range security, reliability, and instructional integration. Ideally, teach undergraduate courses in Computer Science and Cyber Defense , such as Network Security, Ethical Hacking, or Digital Forensics. This position requires a passion for student mentorship, hands-on cybersecurity practice, and applied learning that bridges theory with real-world defense techniques. Qualifications Required Qualifications: Master’s degree in Computer Science, Cybersecurity, Information Technology, or a closely related field . Strong understanding of cybersecurity fundamentals, tools, and competition formats (e.g., NCL, NECCDC, CCDC, CTFtime). Preferred Qualifications: College-level teaching or coaching experience. Industry certifications such as CompTIA Security+, CEH, CISSP, Network+, or equivalent . Experience in managing cybersecurity labs, virtual machines, or practice ranges. Demonstrated ability to mentor students and promote team collaboration. Work Conditions Regular pay rate: $2,145.00 for each 3-hour course, per semester. Higher rates may apply for larger course enrollments, labs, or other duties. Online/remote teaching opportunities may exist dependent on the needs of the course. Applicants interested in online/remote opportunities must reside in the following states: IL, CA, FL, TN, KY. Required Application Materials Cover Letter Resume/CV Copies of transcripts (official required upon hire) Three letters of reference. Equal Opportunity Employer McKendree University is committed to a policy of equal opportunity and prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, and other statuses protected by law. This extends to all aspects of the employment relationship, including recruiting, hiring, training, on-the-job treatment, promotion, layoff, and termination. Part-time employees are not eligible for benefits. Part-time employees who work an average of 20 hours per week may be eligible for our deferred compensation plan. Part-time faculty and staff also enjoy: - Discounted tuition after 1 year of employment ! Spouses and dependents under the age of 26 are also eligible for discounted undergraduate level courses. - Complimentary or discounted tickets to our premier performing arts venue, presenting world class dance, drama, classical music and jazz. - Complimentary tickets for Athletic events. - Discounts at the McKendree University Bookstore. Employer McKendree University Address 701 College Rd Lebanon, Illinois, 62254 Website http://www.mckendree.edu Apply"
